# Sloud core

You are working in the Sloud fleet. Org standards live in the `sloud-engineering-standards` repo (`standards/`). When that tree is available (sibling checkout or vendored copy), follow it. Product `AGENTS.md` adds product-only detail.

## Priority

correctness → security → consistency → speed

## Must

- Human owns every merge; you never approve alone
- Read the relevant `standards/*.md` before building
- UI: Bloom — no invented spacing, type metrics, control heights, or z-index (`standards/08-bloom-design-system.md` → https://github.com/vindhq/sloud-bloom)
- Match existing patterns in the repo you’re in
- No secrets in source or prompts
- No new dependencies without explicit approval
- No `any` / suppressed types / disabled lint without approval

## Must not

- Commit, push, or rewrite git history unless the human explicitly asks
- Fork Bloom tokens or invent a parallel design scale
- Be the sole PR reviewer
